<title>NEW ZEALAND: ANZ, Postbank cut NZ variable mortgage rate.</title>
<headline>ANZ, Postbank cut NZ variable mortgage rate.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand lenders ANZ Bank and Postbank, both controlled by Australia's ANZ Bank, said on Monday they would cut their variable mortgage lending rate to 8.95 percent from 9.40 percent.</p>
<p>The banks said the change followed the Reserve Bank of New Zealand's monetary policy statement on Friday, which they believed indicated that recent falls in wholesale market interest rates would be sustained over the coming months.</p>
<p>The cuts are effective from July 1 for new applications and for existing customers from August 7.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
